  "worked_solution": "First, let's rewrite the polynomial equation in the form ${P}_{n}(t)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{h}^{5}-32{h}^{4}-4{h}^{3} & =16{h}^{3}-13{h}^{5} \\\\ 16{h}^{5}-32{h}^{4}-4{h}^{3} & =16{h}^{3} \\\\ 16{h}^{5}-32{h}^{4}-20{h}^{3} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that all of the terms of the polynomial have a common factor of $4{h}^{3}.$ We can factor out the $4{h}^{3}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{h}^{5}-32{h}^{4}-20{h}^{3} & =0 \\\\ 4{h}^{3}(4{h}^{2}-8h-5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the expression $4{h}^{2}-8h-5$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{h}^{3}(4{h}^{2}-8h-5) & =0 \\\\ 4{h}^{3}(2h+1)(2h-5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by applying the zero product rule, the solutions are $h=0,$ $h=-\\frac{1}{2},$ and $h=\\frac{5}{2}.$",
